-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",180,{
[5729]="70025EAC\n1\tCollect hoes (total: 4)\030Collect sickles (total: 4)\030Collect trowels (total: 4)\030Collect hay-forks (total: 4)\tHoes, sickles, trowels, and hay-forks can be found in the fields of the Northcotton Farm. The tools strewn about the Northcotton Farm need to be cleaned up before the market can be opened.\n2\tBring the farm equipment to Milo Longfurrow\tMilo Longfurrow is at the Northcotton Farm. Milo Longfurrow will be pleased to see the tools have been collected.\n",
[5730]="7002607A\n1\tBring sheep back to the pen (total: 4)\tThe sheep have roamed into the fields surrounding the animal-pens. Gerard Deephole asked you to gather the sheep up and bring them back to the pen.\n2\tTalk to Gerard Deephole\tGerard Deephole is at the animal-pens on the Northcotton Farm. Gerard Deephole will want to know all the sheep are back in the pen.\n",
[5731]="70022B33\n1\tDefeat Gaunt Battle-callers (total: 6)\tGaunt Battle-callers can be found within the Flooded Wing of the Great Barrow.\n",
[5732]="7001B6B7\n1\tGauntlet in Dol Guldur\t\n",
[5733]="7000E76C\n1\tDestroy Gauradan-fetishes (total: 10)\tGauradan-fetishes can be found around and within the entrance of the Jä-kuru, south of Pynti-peldot. Heikki has asked you to destroy several Gauradan-fetishes in order to hinder their incursions against the Lossoth of Pynti-peldot.\n2\tTalk to Heikki\tHeikki is at Pynti-peldot, north of the Jä-kuru. You should return at once to Heikki with news of your success.\n",
[5734]="7000F024\n1\tBring the Gauradan-claws to Juha\030Collect Gauradan-claws (total: 10)\tJuha is at Sûri-kylä and Pynti-peldot in Forochel. Juha has asked you to thin the numbers of the Gauredain threatening the Lossoth and to bring him the claws they wield as weapons as proof of your victory.\n",
[5735]="7000989F\n1\tCollect Gauradan-basket\030Collect Gauradan-spear\030Collect a Gauradan-ward\tErchiel has asked you to collect various relics from the camps of the Gauredain. The Gauradan camps lie in the hills to the north of the Eavespires.\n2\tBring the Gauradan-relics to Erchiel\tYou should return to Erchiel with the Gauredain relics. She can be found at the Eavespires, south of the Gauradan encampments.\n",
[5736]="7004A3A7\n1\tRepair Simple Gearworks\tSimple gearworks can be found in Udûn, You should repair gearworks.\n2\tRepair simple gearworks (total: 9)\030Use gears (total: 9)\tSimple gearworks can be found in Udûn, You should repair gearworks.\n3\tCompleted\tCompleted.\n",
[5737]="7004A38E\n1\tCollect gear\tGears and crankshaft can be found in Udûn. You should collect machine parts.\n2\tCollect crankshafts (total: 10)\030Collect gears (total: 10)\tGears and crankshafts can be found in Udûn. You should collect machine parts.\n3\tPonder the situation\tPonder the situation.\n4\tComplete Turning the Gears\030Complete Gear in the Machine\tGearworks can be found throughout Udûn. You should find places to insert the machine parts you have found.\n5\tDecide what to do next\tDecide what to do next.\n6\tComplete The Caretaker\tGoats can be found in Udûn. After accepting the quest \"The Caretaker\", you should shoo away the goats.\n7\tCompleted\tCompleted.\n",
[5738]="70008660\n1\tBring the rough gems to Bothwar\030Collect rough gems (total: 10)\tGem-bearing servants of the Enemy may be found in Maethad, the arena to the east of Gabilshathûr. Bothwar has offered to pay you for any gems you can find on the servants of the Enemy.\n",
[5739]="70037D6E\n1\tDefeat the leader of the invaders in Gemyndsted\tSpeak with Quickbeam to travel to Gemyndsted.\n2\tTalk to Quickbeam\tHaving defeated the leader of the invaders in Gemyndsted, you prepare to return to Quickbeam and inform him of your success. Quickbeam is at Derndingle.\n",
[5740]="70037DC7\n1\tCollect weathered parchment (total: 8)\tCollect weathered parchments from within Gemyndsted.\n",
[5741]="70037DAE\n1\tDefeat invaders within Gemyndsted (total: 20)\tYou should defeat enemies within Gemyndsted and spare the ruins further damage.\n",
[5742]="7001D0D0\n1\tDefeat General Tímurzgrat\tTímurzgrat, the uruk-general of Gathbúrz, may be found at a tower some distance to the north of Thangúlhad. Rodelleth has instructed you to seek out the Black Uruk General Tímurzgrat and defeat him.\n2\tTalk to Rodelleth at Thangúlhad\tRodelleth is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz, south of General Tímurzgrat's tower. You should return at once to Rodelleth with news of your victory against General Tímurzgrat.\n",
[5743]="7005A681\n1\tVarious rocks can be found next to Bráthi at Zidir-nesad. You should choose the correct rock.\t\n2\tPick up the correct rock\tVarious rocks can be found next to Bráthi at Zidir-nesad. You should pick up the correct rock.\n3\tCrack open the rock that you picked up\tYou should crack open the rock that you picked up.\n4\tShow the geode to Bráthi\tBráthi can be found at Zidir-nesad, The Steepset. You should show the geode to Bráthi.\n",
[5744]="70062AAC\n1\tFind Geralt's missing boot somewhere on the edge of the Wadewater, to the north of Mossward\tWenna told you her husband lost his favourite boot on the edge of the Wadewater, to the north of Mossward.\n2\tSearch the pile of mud on the edge of the Wadewater\tA mysterious object in the mud on the edge of the Wadewater could be Geralt's missing boot.\n3\tBring Geralt's favourite boot to his wife Wenna in south-east Mossward\tWenna is outside her home in south-east Mossward.\n4\tBring his missing favourite boot to Geralt by the north gate of Mossward\tWenna's husband Geralt is by the north gate of Mossward.\n",
[5745]="70062AAB\n1\tFind a hobbit in the village of Clegur who might be interested in Geralt's boot\tGeralt hoped you might ask villagers in the Stoor village of Clegur if they might like his once-loved but now least-favourite boot.\n2\tBring the least-favourite boot to Briallen Wynbuch\tBriallen Wynbuch in the village of Clegur is interested in Geralt's old boot.\n3\tBring the delightful little planter to Wenna in south-east Mossward\tWenna is outside her home in south-east Mossward.\n4\tTalk to Geralt by the north gate of Mossward\tGeralt is by the north gate of Mossward.\n",
[5746]="70000DB4\n1\tSearch for Gerebert Took\tGerebert Took's house is west of Tuckborough, at the end of the road. Esilia has asked you to go to Gerebert Took's house and learn why he is late for dinner.\n2\tSearch Gerebert Took's home\tThe inside of Gerebert Took's home is empty and unused. You should search the house for some information that will explain where Gerebert has gone.\n3\tFind Gerebert's journal and bring it to Esilia Took\030Read Gerebert's journal\tEsilia Took can be found near the centre of Tuckborough. As you entered Gerebert Took's bedroom, you spotted a journal on a table on the other side of the room. It may contain clues as to where Gerebert has gotten off to. You should take it to Esilia Took.\n",
[5747]="7002C60D\n1\tRescue Gerfinn\tYou should find Gerfinn the dwarf and help him get back to the mill. Armund believes he headed roughly north of the sawmill to look for materials of some sort.\n2\tTalk to Gerfinn\tYou should speak with Gerfinn at the Limlight Gorge sawmill.\n",
[5748]="7002F540\n1\tCollect Rohirric books in Gerngarth (total: 4)\tRohirric books can be found within Gerngath. Wulfin has asked you to venture within Gerngath and return with several books documenting the history of the Rohirrim.\n2\tTalk to Wulfin\tWulfin is at Harwick. Wulfin will be pleased to see you recovered several Rohirric books from Gerngath.\n",
[5749]="7002F101\n1\tDefeat trolls and Easterlings in Gerngarth (total: 10)\tEasterlings and trolls can be found in Gerngarth. Wulfin asked you to venture to Gerngarth and defeat the Easterlings pillaging the ancient library.\n2\tTalk to Wulfin\tWulfin can be found in Harwick. Wulfin will want to hear the library of Gerngarth is secure.\n",
[5750]="7001BA83\n1\tBring the weapons to Aggie Honeysuckle\030Collect Aggie's bow (quantity: see journal)\030Collect Sam's halberd (quantity: see journal)\030Collect Dale's mace (quantity: see journal)\tThere are Orcs within the Midgewater Pass. Aggie Honeysuckle is at her camp to the west of the Orc-haunts. Aggie Honeysuckle has asked you to find the weapons the Orcs stole from the hunters when they entered the Midgewater Pass.\n",
[5751]="70067C43\n1\tYou are to head south-east to Súlstrok, an encampment of goblins once loyal to the Corsairs. Once there, you are to plant the banner given to you to call forth one of the strongest goblins. This will enable a ritual combat. Win, and the goblin will surrender to the emissary in Jax Phanâl.\t\n2\tTalk to Stúkha\tWith Shakfut Slit-throat defeated you can now return to Rothog's emissary in Jax Phanâl and inform him of your victory.\n",
[5752]="7000B203\n1\tInform War-tyrant Akúlhun that more forces are needed at Lugazag\tCross the Ettenmoors and deliver the message to War-tyrant Akúlhun that Lugazag is in need of reinforcement. Soldier Dumûl ordered you to seek reinforcements for Lugazag. The tower fell to the forces of Angmar, but must be reinforced or it will be summarily lost to the Free People.\n",
[5753]="7000B204\n1\tInform War-tyrant Akúlhun that Tírith Rhaw requires forces\tCross the Ettenmoors and deliver the message to War-tyrant Akúlhun, at Gramsfoot, that Tírith Rhaw is in need of reinforcements. Soldier Gaath ordered you to seek reinforcements for Tírith Rhaw. The tower fell to the forces of Angmar, but must be reinforced or it will be summarily lost to the Free People.\n",
[5754]="7000B201\n1\tInform War-tyrant Akúlhun that more forces are needed at the Grimwood Lumber Camp\tCross the Ettenmoors and deliver the message to War-tyrant Akúlhun that the Grimwood Lumber Camp is in need of reinforcement. Soldier Kraibag ordered you to seek reinforcements for the Grimwood. Though the lumber camp is controlled by Angmar, it must be reinforced or it will be summarily lost to the Free People.\n",
[5755]="7000B202\n1\tInform War-tyrant Akúlhun that more forces are needed at the Isendeep Mine\tCross the Ettenmoors and deliver the message to War-tyrant Akúlhun that the Isendeep Mine is in need of reinforcement. Soldier Baush ordered you to seek reinforcements for the Isendeep. Though the mine is controlled by Angmar, it must be reinforced or it will be summarily lost to the Free Peoples.\n",
[5756]="70008767\n1\tTalk to Bok at Grothum\tBok is at the goblin-village of Grothum located in the north-east stretches of the Ettenmoors. Soldier Faltúrz directed you to make yourself available to the Goblins of Grothum.\n",
[5757]="7001672F\n1\tDefeat White Hand Orcs in the Redhorn Lodes (total: 14)\tWhite Hand Orcs can be found among the structures of the Redhorn Lodes, south-east of the Orc-watch. Ingifast wishes you to thin the numbers of the White Hand Orcs. He fears they will soon become a greater threat.\n2\tTalk to Ingifast at the Orc-watch\tIngifast is at the Orc-watch, north-west of the Redhorn Lodes. Ingifast will be pleased to hear of the defeat of many of the White Hand Orcs inhabiting the Redhorn Lodes.\n",
[5758]="70032C22\n1\tDefeat White Hand Orcs (total: 6)\030Defeat Moria Orcs (total: 6)\tThe Orcs can be found among the structures of the Redhorn Lodes, south-east of the Orc-watch. White Hand Orcs inhabit the northern half, and the Moria Orcs are ravaging the southern half. Ingifast wants you to sow trouble among the Moria and White Hand Orcs in the Redhorn Lodes.\n2\tReturn to Ingifast\tIngifast is camped on the stairs near Orc-watch. Ingifast will be pleased to hear of the defeat of many of the White Hand and Moria Orcs inhabiting the Redhorn Lodes.\n",
[5759]="7002EEF7\n1\tDefeat the drake that stole Sperling's sword\t\n2\tDrakes can be found hunting the aurochs-herds in the southern part of the Entwash Vale. You should hunt for the drake that swallowed Sperling's sword.\t\n3\tSearch the drake's corpse for Sperling's sword\tYou should search the drake's corpse for Sperling's sword.\n",
[5760]="70017B1D\n1\tBlow the champion's horn and proclaim your prowess in Thorin's Hall\030Climb the Steps of Thorin's Hall\tDwalin's throne is in Thorin's Hall, far to the west of Moria. Valthor has instructed you to go forth and boast of your great deeds before the throne of Dwalin.\n2\tTalk to Thrymur at Thorin's Hall\tThrymur is near Dwalin's throne in Thorin's Hall. Speak with him now that you have proclaimed your deeds to all assembled in Thorin's Hall.\n3\tTalk to Valthor at the Shadowed Refuge\tValthor is at the Shadowed Refuge in the Foundations of Stone in Moria, far to the east of Thorin's Hall. Now that you have boasted to the dwarves, return to Valthor.\n",
})
